/*
 * DAY NUMBERING SYSTEM DOCUMENTATION
 * ==================================
 * 
 * IMPORTANT: Day numbers represent the day of the week, NOT calendar dates!
 * 
 * Day 0 = Monday
 * Day 1 = Tuesday  
 * Day 2 = Wednesday
 * Day 3 = Thursday
 * Day 4 = Friday
 * Day 5 = Saturday
 * Day 6 = Sunday
 * 
 * OVERNIGHT FLIGHTS:
 * - A flight that starts on Day 4 (Friday) at 22:30 and ends on Day 5 (Saturday) at 01:30
 *   is stored as TWO separate entries:
 *   1. Day 4: 22:30-00:00 (flight phase)
 *   2. Day 5: 00:00-01:30 (disembarking phase)
 * 
 * - When checking for conflicts, we must consider that:
 *   - Day 4 01:25-01:30 = Saturday 01:25-01:30 (overnight from Friday to Saturday)
 *   - Day 5 00:30-01:30 = Saturday 00:30-01:30 (same day)
 *   - These DO overlap and should conflict!
 * 
 * CONFLICT DETECTION:
 * - Always convert times to absolute minutes since start of week for accurate comparison
 * - Consider day boundaries when checking overnight flights
 * - Remember that Day 4 late night = Day 5 early morning
 */

